-- title:
--   Ergodic Decay Of The Centered Heat Evolution
-- statement:
--   This statement proves ergodicity of the heat semigroup in centered norm.
--
--   Let $V$, $\nu$, $m$, and $U$ satisfy the heat-model assumptions, with $\nu=m.\operatorname{tilted}(-U)$ and $U\in C^2$. For every $u\in L^2(\nu)$,
--   $$\left\|\operatorname{center}_\nu(P_tu)\right\|\longrightarrow0
--   \qquad\text{as }t\to\infty.$$
--   Here $P_t$ is the semigroup generated by the closed weighted gradient operator.
--
--   This supplies the ergodicity hypothesis required by the curvature-to-Poincaré interface and applies to every $L^2(\nu)$ input, not only operator-domain inputs.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The limit is formulated as a filter limit along real $t\to+\infty$; the conclusion concerns the norm of the centered class.
--
